  ('XSGD', 'XSGD', 'monetary-access-rails', 'centralized-stablecoins', 'https://straitsx.com', ARRAY['Ethereum Mainnet']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "XSGD is a fiat-backed Singapore Dollar stablecoin issued by StraitsX, designed to maintain a 1:1 peg to SGD through offchain cash reserves and issuer-controlled redemption, supporting regulated payments and settlement within Singapore and the broader Asia-Pacific region.", "extras": {"Attestation Frequency": "Regular / periodic (issuer-reported)", "Attestation Provider": "Independent third-party auditor", "Blacklisting Capability": "Yes", "Custodian(s)": "Regulated Singapore financial institutions", "Ethereum Deployment": "Yes", "Failure Mode": "Redemption Delays, Issuance Suspension, Contract Freezes", "Fiat Currency Peg": "SGD (Singapore Dollar)", "Historical Regulatory Actions": "None publicly material", "Issuer Jurisdiction": "Singapore", "Issuer Legal Entity": "Xfers Pte. Ltd. (operating as StraitsX)", "Key Dependency Risks": "Singapore Banking Access, Regulatory Policy, Platform Concentration", "Launch Year": "2020", "Maintaining Organization": "StraitsX", "Market Tier": "Tier 3 — Multi-Currency / Regional Fiat Issuer", "Mint/Burn Control": "Centralized / Permissioned", "Peg Mechanism": "Issuer Redemption", "Practitioner Validation Check": "Does peg stability depend on discretionary offchain redemption by the issuer? Yes", "Practitioner’s Note": "XSGD is best analyzed as a regulatory-aligned regional fiat stablecoin: strong MAS oversight and banking integration enhance trust, while liquidity and composability are intentionally constrained relative to USD-dominant stablecoins.", "Primary Regulator(s)": "Monetary Authority of Singapore (MAS)", "Primary Use Case": "SGD On/Off-Ramps, Regional Payments, Exchange Settlement", "Reason for Inclusion": "XSGD meets centralized stablecoin criteria via centrally controlled issuance, offchain fiat backing, and peg stability enforced through legal redemption rat