ons": "European Union (primary), United Kingdom, limited U.S. coverage", "Primary Use Case": "Low-cost onboarding; repeat fiat funding for DeFi and L2 usage", "Primary User Segment": "Retail users; Web3 apps and wallets embedding on-ramps", "Primary Value Flow": "Fiat → Stablecoin / ETH → Ethereum", "Reason for Inclusion": "Ramp qualifies as a Global On-Ramp because its primary value proposition is enabling multi-country fiat → Ethereum asset conversion, with access and onboarding prioritized over trading or settlement.", "Regional Restrictions": "Yes (jurisdiction-specific, non-EU regions more limited)", "Regulatory Model": "Licensed / Partner-Licensed (EU-first regulatory posture)", "Role Relative to Ethereum": "Access Gateway / Distribution Layer", "Supported Crypto Assets": "ETH, major stablecoins (USDC, USDT), select ERC-20 tokens", "Supported Fiat Currencies": "EUR, GBP, USD, and select local European currencies", "Supported Payment Methods": "Bank Transfers (SEPA, Faster Payments), Cards (credit/debit), Local Payment Rails", "Systemic Importance to Ethereum Access": "High (especially for Europe and L2 ecosystems)"}, "source_label": "Global On-Ramps"}'::jsonb),
